1
00:04:10,434 --> 00:04:16,434
Be afraid. Be very afraid.

2
00:08:20,869 --> 00:08:26,869
The Fly is a horror, science fiction film directed by David Cronenberg.

3
00:12:31,304 --> 00:12:37,304
When Seth Brundle makes a huge scientific and technological
breakthrough in teleportation, he decides to test it on himself.

4
00:16:41,739 --> 00:16:47,739
Unbeknownst to him, a common housefly manages to get
inside the device and the two become one.

5
00:20:52,173 --> 00:20:58,173
Seth Brundle, played by Jeff Goldblum.

6
00:25:02,608 --> 00:25:08,608
Veronica Quaife, played by Geena Davis.

7
00:29:13,043 --> 00:29:19,043
Stathis Borans, played by John Getz.

8
00:33:23,478 --> 00:33:29,478
Tawny, played by Joy Boushel.

9
00:37:33,913 --> 00:37:39,913
Dr. Cheevers, played by Leslie Carlson.

10
00:41:44,347 --> 00:41:50,347
Marky, played by George Chuvalo.

11
00:45:54,782 --> 00:46:00,782
The Fly is a 1986 American science fiction body horror film
directed and co-written by David Cronenberg.

12
00:50:05,217 --> 00:50:11,217
Produced by Brooksfilms and distributed by 20th Century Fox, the
film stars Jeff Goldblum, Geena Davis, and John Getz.

13
00:54:15,652 --> 00:54:21,652
Loosely based on George Langelaan's 1957 short story of the same name and the 1958 film of the same name, The Fly tells of an
eccentric scientist who, after one of his experiments goes wrong, slowly turns into a fly-hybrid creature.

14
00:58:26,086 --> 00:58:32,086
The score was composed by Howard Shore and the make-up effects were created
by Chris Walas, along with makeup artist Stephan Dupuis.

15
01:02:36,521 --> 01:02:42,521
The Fly was released on August 15, 1986, to positive reviews.

16
01:06:46,956 --> 01:06:52,956
It grossed $60.6 million at the box office, becoming a commercial success.

17
01:10:57,391 --> 01:11:03,391
Walas and Dupuis' work on the film resulted in them
winning an Academy Award for Best Makeup.

18
01:15:07,826 --> 01:15:13,826
The tagline of the film, "Be afraid.

19
01:19:18,260 --> 01:19:24,260
Be very afraid.", has been used in many other
productions as part of popular culture.

20
01:23:28,695 --> 01:23:34,695
A sequel, directed by Walas, was released in 1989.

21
01:27:39,130 --> 01:27:45,130
The film explores themes of monster, experiment,
mutation, toronto, canada, mutant.

22
01:31:49,565 --> 01:31:55,565
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
